  "summary_en": "AI Forum of New Zealand's 2018 report analysing AI's potential economic and societal impact on New Zealand. It maps the AI landscape, estimates economic benefits ($22.5–53.6bn by 2035) and labour market effects, and recommends a coordinated national AI strategy, skills development and ongoing ethical and legal discussion.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI could add NZ$22.5–53.6 billion to the NZ economy by 2035 through labour substitution and efficiency.",
   "Calls for a cohesive national AI strategy, comparing NZ with Canada, UK, China, Estonia, Singapore and France.",
   "Highlights labour market disruption and need for reskilling and lifelong learning.",
   "Supports ongoing discussion of practical ethical and legal principles for AI.",
   "Barriers to adoption include skills shortages and data access; IoT adoption seen as a foundation."
